[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3497367290","pull_request_review_id":4598754831,"id":3497367290,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7QdZb6","diff_hunk":"@@ -913,7 +914,12 @@ void ParticleProcessMaterial::_update_shader() {\n \tcode += \"\tuint base_number = NUMBER;\\n\";\n \tcode += \"\tuint alt_seed = hash(base_number + uint(1) + RANDOM_SEED);\\n\";\n \tcode += \"\tDisplayParameters params;\\n\";\n-\tcode += \"\tcalculate_initial_display_params(params, alt_seed);\\n\";\n+\tif (PARTICLE_FLAG_PRESERVE_COLOR) {\n+\t\tcode += \"\t\tUSERDATA2 = COLOR;\\n\";","path":"scene/resources/particle_process_material.cpp","commit_id":"01ca4c224670eb88024f682b59d63d4476d58c8b","original_commit_id":"01ca4c224670eb88024f682b59d63d4476d58c8b","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"```suggestion\n\t\tcode += \"\tUSERDATA2 = COLOR;\\n\";\n```\nI presume?","created_at":"2026-06-30T08:42:35Z","updated_at":"2026-06-30T08:43:51Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120764#discussion_r3497367290","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120764","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3497367290"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120764#discussion_r3497367290"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120764"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3497367290/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":918,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":25,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3499551632","pull_request_review_id":4601303824,"id":3499551632,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7QluuQ","diff_hunk":"@@ -649,7 +649,8 @@ void ParticleProcessMaterial::_update_shader() {\n \tcode += \"\tparams.animation_speed = mix(anim_speed_min, anim_speed_max, rand_from_seed(alt_seed));\\n\";\n \tcode += \"\tparams.animation_offset = mix(anim_offset_min, anim_offset_max, rand_from_seed(alt_seed));\\n\";\n \tcode += \"\tparams.lifetime = (1.0 - lifetime_randomness * rand_from_seed(alt_seed));\\n\";\n-\tcode += \"\tparams.color = color_value;\\n\";\n+\tcode += \"\tparams.color = color_value * color_multiplier;\\n\";","path":"scene/resources/particle_process_material.cpp","commit_id":"85d7cdb8592f7a3300aae77051ef63befb097536","original_commit_id":"85d7cdb8592f7a3300aae77051ef63befb097536","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I haven’t looked into this much at all, so I am not aware of whether `params.color` and `color_multiplier` use nonlinear sRGB encoding or linear encoding. This implications of this are as follows:\n\n1. If there is a mismatch between the two variables (maybe with the HDR 2D setting or 3D vs 2D rendering), you will get unexpected results.\n2. If both use nonlinear sRGB encoding, then the contrast (and hue and saturation) of the colour will be affected by this math. For example, multiplying a nonlinear sRGB colour by 0.1 will reduce the contrast of an image and reduce the saturation of the colour because of the colour channels converging near zero from the nonlinear encoding.\n3. If both use linear encoding, then simple brightness adjustments will be somewhat less intuitive to the user because multiplying by 0.5 will not produce 50% brightness, but the contrast of the image and hue and saturation of the colours will be preserved, as the multiplication will be a linear operation.\n\nOther things to consider is whether behaviour changes between the HDR 2D setting or between other rendering configurations (some use linear other use nonlinear sRGB).\n\nAnyway, this stuff is more complicated than it might seem on the surface due to how Godot uses colour maths on both of these encodings, so I wanted to point out the implications so that the right decision can be made on this PR.","created_at":"2026-06-30T14:34:32Z","updated_at":"2026-06-30T14:34:32Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120764#discussion_r3499551632","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120764","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3499551632"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120764#discussion_r3499551632"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120764"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3499551632/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":652,"original_line":652,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":14,"position":14,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3504151176","pull_request_review_id":4606848673,"id":3504151176,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7Q3RqI","diff_hunk":"@@ -649,7 +649,8 @@ void ParticleProcessMaterial::_update_shader() {\n \tcode += \"\tparams.animation_speed = mix(anim_speed_min, anim_speed_max, rand_from_seed(alt_seed));\\n\";\n \tcode += \"\tparams.animation_offset = mix(anim_offset_min, anim_offset_max, rand_from_seed(alt_seed));\\n\";\n \tcode += \"\tparams.lifetime = (1.0 - lifetime_randomness * rand_from_seed(alt_seed));\\n\";\n-\tcode += \"\tparams.color = color_value;\\n\";\n+\tcode += \"\tparams.color = color_value * color_multiplier;\\n\";","path":"scene/resources/particle_process_material.cpp","commit_id":"85d7cdb8592f7a3300aae77051ef63befb097536","original_commit_id":"85d7cdb8592f7a3300aae77051ef63befb097536","user":{"login":"QbieShay","id":7917475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MTc0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7917475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay","html_url":"https://github.com/QbieShay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I am not sure this is within the scope of this PR. This is just feeding back data that Godot already passes into the shader. What this fixes is that the color passed into the shader is preserved instead of discarded, but this is not user input, the color is already processed by Godot\n\n`emit_particle` is preserved. whatever conversion happens there, we should perhaps look into together?\n\ni know there are issues for 2d for color conversion (things are darker than they should iirc)","created_at":"2026-07-01T07:51:28Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T07:51:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120764#discussion_r3504151176","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120764","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3504151176"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120764#discussion_r3504151176"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120764"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3504151176/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":652,"original_line":652,"side":"RIGHT