\r\n...But if this PR just allows the colour provided by `emit_particle(...)` to be preserved, then why isn't it like:\r\n\r\n```\r\nif (preserve_color) {\r\n    params.color = preserved_color;\r\n} else {\r\n    params.color = color_value;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt seems the `color` parameter in `emit_particle(...)` doesn't work at all before this PR? Or is there a case where this sort of multiplied `color * color` exists that I can look into as a reference?","created_at":"2026-07-06T00:05:20Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T00:05:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120764#discussion_r3525877667","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120764","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3525877667"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120764#discussion_r3525877667"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120764"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3525877667/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":652,"original_line":652,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3499551632,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":14,"position":14,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3544552539","pull_request_review_id":4654820631,"id":3544552539,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7TRZRb","diff_hunk":"@@ -649,7 +649,8 @@ void ParticleProcessMaterial::_update_shader() {\n \tcode += \"\tparams.animation_speed = mix(anim_speed_min, anim_speed_max, rand_from_seed(alt_seed));\\n\";\n \tcode += \"\tparams.animation_offset = mix(anim_offset_min, anim_offset_max, rand_from_seed(alt_seed));\\n\";\n \tcode += \"\tparams.lifetime = (1.0 - lifetime_randomness * rand_from_seed(alt_seed));\\n\";\n-\tcode += \"\tparams.color = color_value;\\n\";\n+\tcode += \"\tparams.color = color_value * color_multiplier;\\n\";","path":"scene/resources/particle_process_material.cpp","commit_id":"85d7cdb8592f7a3300aae77051ef63befb097536","original_commit_id":"85d7cdb8592f7a3300aae77051ef63befb097536","user":{"login":"QbieShay","id":7917475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MTc0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7917475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay","html_url":"https://github.com/QbieShay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It doesn't work at all with Process Material. What you can do is to make a particle shader that does not use Process Material.\r\n\r\n> ...But if this PR just allows the colour provided by emit_particle(...) to be preserved, then why isn't it like:\r\n\r\nBecause we still want to combine the color with the given color in ProcessMaterial, otherwise it will look wrong.","created_at":"2026-07-08T13:57:24Z","updated_at":"2026-07-08T13:57:24Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120764#discussion_r3544552539","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120764","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3544552539"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120764#discuss